# Paamayim (נהורא): Design Rules

This project is an Expo SDK 52 + expo-router app (React Native 0.76, Hebrew RTL). We are restyling it, one screen at a time, to match a mockup. These rules always apply.

## 1. Do-not-touch list (hard rules)

Never modify these unless the user's message explicitly names the file and the change:

1. `src/components/SideMenu.tsx`: no code, style, animation or content changes at all. (The only allowed edit, already done: `export` on `MenuItem`, `MENU_ITEMS`, `isItemActive` so `WideMenu` reuses the same items.) The phone menu is always this component.
2. `src/components/MenuButton.tsx`: keep the component exactly as is. Every screen keeps rendering `<MenuButton />` on the **visual right side of its header**, the same as today (phone layout). On wide web (≥768) the MenuButton lives in `TopNav` instead.
3. `src/components/GlassBottomNav.tsx`: may be restyled visually only. Keep the 4 items, their order, labels and routes (בית `/(tabs)`, מסלול `/(tabs)/path`, משפחה `/(tabs)/family`, עוד `/(tabs)/more`), navigation with `router.push`, and the exports `GlassBottomNav` and `BOTTOM_NAV_SPACE = 96`. Style: glass card radius 24, lucide line icons (House, Map, Users, Ellipsis), the active item on a soft white tile. Only the current screen's item is active. A screen may hide the nav by passing `showNav={false}` to the background wrapper.
4. `app/(tabs)/more.tsx` (the "עוד" screen): may be restyled visually only. Keep every action exactly: calendar choice (israel/diaspora), "פתח תפריט ניווט" (openSideMenu), "מסך פתיחה מחדש" (setOnboardingDone(false)), "משפטי" (/legal), "איפוס התקדמות" (same Alert, resetProgress + setOnboardingDone(false); on wide web `window.confirm`, because `Alert.alert` shows nothing in a browser), and the version footer. The wide layout (`MoreWide`) adds a "הגדרות" row. Both layouts add `PersonalCard` (the personal page: optional name) and a "כל הפרשות" row (→ `/parashot`); `MoreWide` also shows `GreetingHeader`.
5. The "התחל" button on the splash/onboarding branch of `app/(tabs)/index.tsx`: keep its styles exactly (`styles.startBtn`, `styles.startFill`, `styles.startText`, `styles.startArrow`, the BlurView and the chevron). Only its `onPress` may change when a step says so.
6. `src/components/TorahScrollView.tsx` and `assets/megillah-*.png`: the scroll's look stays as it is. The only additions are the optional props `currentVerseId` (highlight `tsv-<id>` + auto-scroll) and `onVersePress` (tap a verse to jump). Without them it renders exactly as before. The scroll always shows the **current aliyah** (never the story/focus verses).
7. Brand: the app name stays **נהורא**. Do not edit `src/theme/brand.ts` (`APP_NAME = 'נהורא'`, `APP_TAGLINE = 'אור הפסוק. עד שבת.'`). Never write "NuraWell" in the UI.
8. `src/theme/tokens.ts` and `src/theme/fonts.ts`: never change existing values (SideMenu depends on `colors`, `radii`, `spacing`, `assets.galilee`, `assets.icon`). New tokens go only in `src/theme/design.ts`.
9. Data and state logic: `src/store/useAppStore.ts` and `src/data/*` must not change existing behavior. Additive changes only (new optional fields / actions, persisted). Already added: `completeVerse`, `pickedParashaId`, `userName`, `namePromptDismissed` (store); `weekSedra` / `isAfterShabbat` in `parashot.ts` (skip chag weeks, move to next week after motzaei Shabbat — covered by `npm run test:dates`); optional `Verse.onkelosExplanation`, `Verse.chidushim`, `Parasha.extras`, `HaftaraInfo.whyThisHaftaraChild` (types). Haftara content may change as before.
10. Existing files in `assets/` (root) must not be deleted, renamed or overwritten.

## 2. Platform scope and responsive web

- **Phone layout** (native phones, and web < 768px) is the reference design. It must stay pixel-identical: the phone code path of every screen is the original component (e.g. `HomeMobile`, `PathMobile`) and is not changed by web work.
- The app must still run in Expo Go (iOS/Android) and in a mobile browser (`expo start --web` at 393×852).
- `npx tsc --noEmit` must pass after every change.

### Breakpoints (web and native), shared hook `src/ui/useLayout.ts`

| Breakpoint | Width | Layout |
|---|---|---|
| phone | < 768 | current mobile design, bottom tab bar (`GlassBottomNav`) |
| tablet | 768–1199 (native: ≥ 700dp) | top nav (`TopNav`), 2 columns where it helps, gutters 32 |
| desktop | ≥ 1200 | top nav with full labels + settings button, 2–4 column grids, gutters 48 |

- `const { bp, isWide, isNativeTablet, isDesktop, isTablet, gutter, contentMax } = useLayout()`. `isWide = bp !== 'phone'` on every platform: web ≥ 768, native ≥ 700dp (iPad mini portrait 744 qualifies; phones and folded foldables don't). Native tablets therefore get the wide layout too — use `rtl` helpers in wide code, never raw left/right/row. Wide `ScreenBackground` respects safe-area insets. Note: `app.json` orientation is still `portrait`.
- Tokens: `nw.layout` (`tablet` 768, `desktop` 1200, `contentMax` 1200, `gutterTablet` 32, `gutterDesktop` 48, `textMax` 680, `topNavH` 68) and `nw.type.displayWide`.
- Pattern per screen: the default export only picks the branch, e.g. `return isWide ? <PathWide /> : <PathMobile />;`. Never add an early return after other hooks. Wide screens live in `src/wide/*` (or next to the mobile component in the same route file for small ones), and reuse `src/ui` components and the same store/data.
- Wide pages use `WidePage` (`src/ui/WidePage.tsx`): background A + `TopNav`, content centered with `maxWidth` ≤ 1200, large page title (`displayWide` on desktop), optional back button. Content is vertically centered when shorter than the window (no empty bottom half on a 820×1180 tablet). On tablet prefer stacking (wide image on top, text below) over two thin columns — see `StoryWide`. Columns: `WideCols` (RTL row, `stack` to collapse). Section headings: `WideSectionTitle`.
- Screens that keep the phone layout on wide web (settings, legal, splash, calendar) use `ScreenBackground` props `wideMaxWidth` (centered column) and `wideNav` (show `TopNav`). The photo and scrim stay full-bleed.
- Wide home (`src/wide/HomeHero.tsx`): centered leaf + greeting (line 1/2) + status sentence, then a row of glass feature cards — desktop 5 (סיפור הפרשה, מסלול, **פרשת השבוע**, סיפור ההפטרה, משפחה), tablet 3 — where the central parasha card is larger, `variant="frost"` and glows (soft teal shadow, brighter border); then the status CTA, "כל הפרשות" pill, and the WaveBand. Phone home is unchanged by this.
- `TopNav` is a floating pill (radius = height/2); the active link is shown by a teal underline only (hover = faint pearl); desktop adds a solid teal CTA pill "לקריאה" at the far left.
- Navigation on wide layouts: `TopNav` replaces the bottom tab bar. It uses the same routes (`NAV_ITEMS` / `isNavActive` exported from `GlassBottomNav`), the brand נהורא on the right, a calendar pill (→ `/calendar`), settings (desktop) and `MenuButton`. On wide layouts `SideMenuHost` renders `WideMenu` (`src/components/WideMenu.tsx`): a **full-screen** glass overlay over the Galilee photo, brand block, grid of large tiles (3 columns desktop / 2 tablet, 26px bold titles, active tile highlighted) built from `MENU_ITEMS` / `isItemActive`, close button top-left and **Esc** to close. On phone it renders the unchanged `SideMenu`. `ScreenHeader` hides its own menu button on wide layouts.
- Text line length: paragraphs ≤ `nw.layout.textMax` (680) via `wideText(style)`. Never stretch buttons full width on wide: CTAs are max 320–520 wide.
- Hover (web, mouse only): `GlassSurface` with `onPress` lifts 2px with `shadow.float`; TopNav links get a soft white background. Touch never triggers hover.
- Reading on desktop shows verse card (`large`) and Torah scroll side by side (scroll column 472 wide, height follows the window; current verse highlighted, tap a verse to jump). Tablet keeps the verse/scroll toggle; scroll mode adds `ScrollReadBar`. Keyboard: ← next verse, → previous verse, Enter = "קראתי שניים ואחד" + next.
- Olive-branch edge art: `src/ui/OliveBranches.tsx` (rendered by wide `ScreenBackground`, `pointerEvents="none"`), images `img.oliveLeft` / `img.oliveRight` (transparent PNGs ≤ 400KB). Sized from the free side margin so they never overlap content; hidden on phone. The background stays `img.mistSky` (wide: `contentPosition: 'bottom'`).

### Home header (phone)

- The home header floats over the hero image: `HeroBanner underlay={insets.top + 56 + 8}` extends the image behind the status bar and header, with a soft top scrim `nw.header.scrim`. The header is transparent at rest and fades in a frosted gradient (`nw.header.frost`, no hard bottom edge) after scrolling `nw.header.frostFadeAt` (90) px. Content below the banner keeps its exact position.

## 3. Working rules

- Make only the change the current step asks for. Do not refactor unrelated code, rename files, reformat untouched files or "clean up" other screens.
- New reusable UI goes in `src/ui/` and is exported from `src/ui/index.ts`. Old components in `src/components/` stay. Stop using them in a screen only when that screen is restyled.
- No hard-coded hex colors, font sizes, radii or shadows inside screens. Use `nw` from `src/theme/design.ts`. (Exception: the Israel flag SVG colors.)
- After finishing a screen, compare it with its mockup image in `design/mockup/` and list any remaining visual differences in your reply.
- Do **not** run `git commit`, `git push`, or create branches/PRs unless the user explicitly asks.
- Do not install packages other than: `react-native-svg`, `expo-image` (via `npx expo install`), `lucide-react-native` (via npm), and the dev-only `esbuild` (used by `npm run test:dates`). The admin app in `admin/` has its own `package.json`.

