| `GreetingHeader` / `NamePrompt` | time greeting + day greeting (2nd line), "כל הפרשות" pill, "חזרה לפרשת השבוע" when a parasha is picked; gentle skippable name prompt |
| `PersonalCard` | "הפרטים שלך": optional name (stored only on the device) + greeting preview; used in עוד and settings |
| `OliveBranches` | wide-only side-margin olive art |

## 10. Reading session (שניים מקרא ואחד תרגום)

- All reading logic lives in `src/reading/useReadingSession.ts`, shared by `app/reading.tsx` (phone) and `src/wide/ReadingWide.tsx`. Never duplicate it in a screen.
- Primary action is one tap: "קראתי שניים ואחד · לפסוק הבא" (`completeVerse` sets all three passes) and auto-advance. The single tiles stay for partial progress.
- Resume: without params the session opens on `lastVerseId`'s aliyah. Progress shown per aliyah ("x/y" + bar).
- Focus mode (`?focus=` story verses) is a side trip: it shows `FocusBanner`, never overwrites `lastVerseId`, and the Torah scroll still shows the current aliyah.
- Bonus content (Onkelos explanation, chidushim) sits under the verse, never between the user and the CTA.

## 11. Content system

- Content lives as JSON in `content/parashot/<slug>.json` (schema `content/schema.json`). Each field is `{ published, draft, updatedAt, publishedAt, source }`; the app only ever sees `published`. Edit through the admin app (`admin/`), not by hand.
- `npm run content:build` → `public/content/index.json` + `public/content/parashot/*.json` (git-ignored) and `src/content/bundled.json` (offline fallback, committed). `build:web` runs it automatically.
- Runtime (`src/content/`): bundled → AsyncStorage cache → fetch `EXPO_PUBLIC_CONTENT_BASE_URL` (web default: same origin). Screens read the parasha only through `useParasha(mode)` (respects the picked parasha) and helpers `lifeLessonsFor`, `contentImage`, `whyHaftaraFor`, `useParashaEyebrow`. Never import `getCurrentParasha` directly in a screen.
- `app/parashot.tsx` is the parasha picker (grouped by book, "חזרה לפרשת השבוע"). Picking sets `pickedParashaId`; the home hero then says "הפרשה שבחרת" instead of "פרשת השבוע".
- `npm run content:import` imports the content-writer worker output as drafts (never published automatically).
- API keys only in `admin/.env` (never committed; `admin/.env.example` documents them).

## 12. Greetings

- Every greeting text lives in `src/greeting/texts.ts` (single editable file). Logic in `src/greeting/greeting.ts`, hook `useGreeting()`.
- Line 1 is always the time greeting by local hour (06–11:59 בוקר טוב, 12–15:59 צהריים טובים, 16–16:59 אחר הצהריים טובים, 17–20:59 ערב טוב, 21–05:59 לילה טוב) + optional name + 👋. Line 2 is the day greeting (שבת שלום from Friday 12:00, שבוע טוב from motzaei Shabbat to Sunday 12:00, holidays, Rosh Chodesh). The day greeting never replaces the time greeting.
- Memorial days (יום השואה, יום הזיכרון, יום הזיכרון לחללי מלחמת חרבות ברזל, ז׳ באוקטובר, תשעה באב): no emoji, line 2 is the respectful sentence.
- Below the greeting on home: `HomeStatus` — a personal status sentence + live progress bar + CTA (`useStatusLine`). Sentences (100, by category: notStarted, midway, almostDone, finished, returning, friday, holiday) live in `content/greetings/status-lines.json`, each neutral or `{m,f,p}`, placeholders `{name} {parasha} {aliyah} {remaining} {done} {left} {percent}`. Hebrew number words via `src/greeting/hebrewNumbers.ts` (עלייה ראשונה, שש עליות, נשארה עוד עלייה אחת).
- Rotation: a new sentence on app open / refresh / return to home (focus), stable while shown, never the same as the previous one (`statusLast` in the store). Progress numbers update live; when the category changes (e.g. just finished) it switches immediately.
- Gender (optional, `userGender`): גבר → m, אישה → f, ״מעדיף/ה לא לשתף״ or unset → plural. Every second-person UI text goes through `g()` / `useG()` (`src/greeting/gender.ts`, `useG.ts`) with variants in `src/greeting/uiTexts.ts`. Never hard-code a gendered "המשך/קרא/סיימת" in a screen.
- Any change to dates/greetings/status must keep `npm test` (alias `npm run test:dates`) green.

## 13. Accessibility, privacy, security

- Every `Pressable`/touchable has `accessibilityRole` + a Hebrew `accessibilityLabel` (state via `accessibilityState`). Decorative images/backdrops are not focusable.
- Text contrast ≥ 4.5:1 (WCAG AA) on every surface incl. frost 0.30 over the photo/sky: body text `ink`/`inkSoft`, secondary `inkMuted`, teal text `tealText` (never `tealIcon`/`tealBright` for text), warnings `dangerText`. White text only on `teal`/`tealText` (≥ 6:1).
- Font scaling: system font scaling is allowed up to `MAX_FONT_SCALE` (1.5, `capFontScaling()` in `src/utils/a11y.ts`). Prefer `minHeight` over fixed `height` for anything with text.
- Web: `applyWebA11y()` sets `lang="he"`, a visible `:focus-visible` ring (3px `tealText`) and honours `prefers-reduced-motion`. Do not set `dir="rtl"` on the document (layout is LTR + `rtl.row`). In JS animations use `prefersReducedMotion()` / `motionMs()` (`src/ui/reducedMotion.ts`); `useNativeDriver` only off-web.
- Screen-reader order = DOM order = visual right-to-left (rtl.row), so keep the main item first in code.
- Privacy: name, gender and progress live only in the device store (AsyncStorage/localStorage). No analytics, ads, tracking or crash-reporting SDKs. `PrivacyNote` (legal screen + "הפרטים שלך") explains it and offers "מחיקת הפרטים האישיים" (`clearPersonalData`). Copy lives in `PRIVACY` (`src/greeting/texts.ts`).
- Security: no secrets in the app — anything `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` ships to every user. Remote content is validated (size cap, slug regex, object shape); content image URIs must be `https://` or a safe relative path (resolved against the content server). `public/_headers` sets security headers on Cloudflare Pages. `.env*` is git-ignored except `.env.example`.
- Wide home hero tree: `WIDE_HERO_TREE` in `src/wide/heroTree.ts` — `'none'` (default, no tree), `'background'` (soft faded tree behind the cards, `home-hero-tree-soft.webp`) or `'card'` (small tree image at the top of the glowing "פרשת השבוע" card, `home-hero-tree-thumb.webp`). One-line switch; phone is not affected.
- No pure white surfaces: cards are glass (`GlassSurface`), inputs use `nw.surface.input` (pearl 0.40) with a soft teal border. `#FFFFFF` only for text/icons on teal. The name prompt is `frost` glass and centered.

## 14. Admin app (`admin/`)

- Run: `npm run admin` (installs, creates `admin/.env` with a hashed password, builds, starts on `127.0.0.1:8787`). Dev: `npm --prefix admin run dev`. Docs: `admin/README.md` (Hebrew), `admin/API.md`.
- Server (Hono, Node ≥ 20.19): no DB. `STORAGE=local` writes files in the repo (atomic, realpath-checked); `STORAGE=github` commits through the Git Data API (one commit per save, draft saves carry `[CF-Pages-Skip]`). Only paths whitelisted in `admin/server/paths.ts` can be written.
- Forms are generated from `content/schema.json` — a new field in the schema appears in the admin automatically. Everything is saved as a draft; publishing (per field / per parasha / all verse explanations) also rebuilds `src/content/bundled.json` via `buildOutputs()` in `scripts/content/lib.mjs`.
- Security: scrypt password hash, signed HttpOnly SameSite=Strict cookie (Secure when hosted), CSRF header + Origin check on every mutation, rate limits (login 5/min + 30/h, API 600/min, AI 20/min), body limits, image validation + WebP re-encode, CSP/security headers. Optional `ADMIN_API_TOKEN` (Bearer) for a dashboard.
- AI keys only in `admin/.env`, never sent to the browser. Bulk jobs need a signed cost estimate first and are capped by `AI_MAX_JOB_USD`. Never overwrite a published value — AI output is always a draft.
- UI: same pearl/glass language as the app, Assistant + Frank Ruhl Libre, RTL, top pill nav on desktop and bottom nav ≤ 760px. Every control has a visible label or `aria-label`, focus ring, keyboard shortcuts (Ctrl+S, Ctrl+Enter, Alt+←/→). Keep axe (WCAG 2.1 AA) clean.

